# hearth's model: Unsloth's UD-Q4_K_XL build of Google's QAT Gemma 4 26B-A4B (docs/model-scorecard.md).
# Pulled from Hugging Face it gets a generic template, so thinking and tool calls aren't separated;
# Gemma's renderer and parser fix that, with Gemma's sampling settings and hearth's 64k window
# (HEARTH_NUM_CTX: a different num_ctx makes Ollama reload the model between callers).
#
# DRAFT is Google's speculative-decoding assistant for this QAT checkpoint: it guesses the next tokens
# and the model checks every one, so answers don't change (the French bench gave identical answers on
# all 458 items). It must be the QAT assistant; the non-QAT one was slower than none. DRAFT takes a file,
# never a model name, so it points at the pulled assistant's blob (Ollama's Linux service store; on a
# Mac, ~/.ollama/models/blobs). `ollama create` copies it into the tag, so it is read only here.
# draft_num_predict 2: Ollama's default of 4 was slower than no assistant at temperature 1.
#   ollama pull hf.co/unsloth/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-qat-GGUF:UD-Q4_K_XL
#   ollama pull hf.co/mradermacher/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-qat-q4_0-unquantized-assistant-GGUF:Q4_K_M
#   ollama create gemma4-26b-a4b-ud-64k -f deploy/ollama/gemma4-26b-a4b-ud-64k.Modelfile
FROM hf.co/unsloth/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-qat-GGUF:UD-Q4_K_XL
DRAFT /usr/share/ollama/.ollama/models/blobs/sha256-b4ee308edc095cba54a47e15a2113d83d451253593c5cceede27a31ccf6c91a3
RENDERER gemma4
PARSER gemma4
TEMPLATE {{ .Prompt }}
PARAMETER temperature 1
PARAMETER top_k 64
PARAMETER top_p 0.95
PARAMETER num_ctx 65536
PARAMETER draft_num_predict 2
